## Consolidate Lakebase technical access into a shared subpackage

Context: The psycopg connection pool was duplicated between the registry store
(`back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py`) and the graph engine
(`back/core/graphdb/lakebase/pool.py`) — the latter's docstring even said so.
Auth (`LakebaseAuth`) and grants (`lakebase_grants.py`) already lived under
`back/core/databricks/`. This extracts one technical access layer shared by
both consumers while keeping the Registry and Triple Store as two independent
databases (each supplies its own auth + schema + database; pools never merge).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/constants.py
   New: cold-start SQLSTATEs, retry/backoff, pool sizing, JWT TTL, and the
   `ontobricks-registry` / `ontobricks-graphdb` workload labels.
2. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/psycopg_gate.py
   New: `require_psycopg()` — the single lazy-import gate (raises ImportError).
3. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseConnectionPool.py
   New: unified `LakebaseConnectionPool`, `get_lakebase_pool(auth, schema,
   database, *, application_name, error_factory)`, `lakebase_cursor()`, and
   `LakebaseConnectionError`. Pool key is the full connection identity plus the
   workload label, so different projects/databases/schemas never share a pool.
4. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/LakebaseAuth.py (moved from parent)
   `LakebaseAuth` / `BranchLakebaseAuth` / `get_lakebase_auth`; token TTL now
   sourced from `constants.TOKEN_TTL_S`.
5. src/back/core/databricks/lakebase/Grants.py (moved from lakebase_grants.py)
   Reusable grant primitives, unchanged.
6. src/back/core/databricks/LakebaseAuth.py, src/back/core/databricks/lakebase_grants.py
   Now backward-compat shims re-exporting from the subpackage (test monkeypatch
   targets and existing imports preserved).
7. src/back/core/graphdb/lakebase/pool.py
   Reduced to a shim: `get_lakebase_graph_pool` / `_require_psycopg` /
   `LakebaseGraphPoolError` delegate to the shared layer (graph label).
8. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py
   Deleted the embedded `_LakebasePool` + duplicated constants/helpers; `_get_pool`
   and `_require_psycopg` are now thin wrappers over the shared layer (registry
   label, errors wrapped as `StoreError`). Behaviour identical.
9. src/back/core/databricks/__init__.py
   Re-export `LakebaseAuth` / `get_lakebase_auth` from the subpackage.
10. docs/code_organization.md
   Documented the `databricks/lakebase/` subpackage in the `back/core` tree.

