## Fix full-suite failures from Playwright/asyncio event-loop clash

Context: A bare ``pytest -q`` run failed 51 MCP/API tests with
``RuntimeError: Cannot run the event loop while another loop is running``.
``tests/e2e/scenarios/test_full_lifecycle.py`` was not gated by the nightly
e2e skip (only non-scenario e2e tests were), so it started the session-scoped
Playwright loop during routine full-suite runs.

Changes:

1. tests/e2e/conftest.py
   Skip **all** ``tests/e2e/**`` tests (including scenarios) unless e2e/scenario
   is explicitly targeted; treat ``-m "not scenario"`` as non-explicit.
2. tests/units/test_e2e_collection_gating.py
   Unit tests for ``_e2e_explicitly_selected`` marker/path detection.

